      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it sounds out there, but i'm literally measuring the barometric pressure shifts in my studio when the sequence hits. it's not just \"mood,\" it's a physical modulation of the space. if we look at it from a bio-resonance perspective—like how certain frequencies can trigger entrainment in brainwaves—surely there has to be a mathematical threshold where sound stops being just \"audio\" and starts acting as a direct stimulus for neural intention? if i can find the math behind that threshold, i can basically architect the environment to force a state of absolute focus.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
